# Story: on a MacBook Air someone has Mail on the left and Notes beside it. Notes will not go under 709 points, more than its share,
# so Arbor has borrowed the rest from the Desktop on its right (F61). They want Notes wider still and drag the gap between Mail and
# Notes 60 points to the left. That is their word on the arrangement: nothing Arbor does by itself takes it back.
# (It used to: the 60 points counted as points Notes could spare, and went to the Desktop at the next layout.)
# Reference: T05 T20, F61; rules 2 and 7 of issue #3.
# The Desktop has a share of its own beside the docked windows, as in the first build: it is the lender of this story.
set desktopColumn true
# As Arbor ships, what cannot fit overlaps (F69). This story is about the tile, which is an option now.
set windowsThatDoNotFit tile
open Mail 900x600
open Notes 1000x660 min 709x300
dock 101 left
dock 102 beside 101 right
expect size 101 348x851
expect size 102 709x851
seam 0 -60
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
# ⌃⌥0 at home, Show Everything, a look at one window and back, a look at the Desktop and back.
press home
expect size 102 769x851
press show-all
expect size 102 769x851
zoom 101
back
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
desktop
show-all
expect size 102 769x851
# A window opens and closes.
open Calculator 230x408
expect size 102 769x851
close 103
expect size 102 769x851
# Mail goes into the Dock and comes back; it is hidden and shown.
minimize 101
restore 101
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
hide Mail
unhide Mail
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
# A pause gives both their own sizes back, and the end of it the arrangement as it was left.
pause
expect size 102 1000x660
resume
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
# Quit, and start again.
relaunch
expect size 101 288x851
expect size 102 769x851
home
expect size 102 769x851
# The next drag starts where the last one ended, by the window's own edge and by command as by the gap.
pull 101 right -20
expect size 102 789x851
home
expect size 102 789x851
resize 102 left 11
home
expect size 101 257x851
expect size 102 800x851
# The other way: squeezed below its smallest size on purpose, Notes is the tile they asked for, as wide as they left it.
focus 101
seam 0 200
expect tile 102
expect size 101 457x851
home
show-all
zoom 101
back
expect tile 102
expect size 101 457x851
# The same hand lets it out again, and there it stays.
seam 0 -150
expect visible 102
expect size 102 750x851
home
expect size 102 750x851
# What ends it: the windows in the arrangement change.
close 102
expect visible 101
expect count docked 1
# Another desk. Mail will not go under 400 points and a wide table not under 900, so the Desktop has given all it can: it is a tile,
# and Arbor owes it room. They want the table wider still, and pay for it with Mail, which becomes the tile they asked for.
close 101
open Mail 900x600 min 400x300
open Numbers 1000x660 min 900x300
dock 104 left
dock 105 beside 104 right
expect size 104 400x851
expect size 105 900x851
focus 105
seam 0 -160
expect tile 104
expect size 105 1060x851
# The points they gave to the table are not the Desktop's to take, nor what they left to Mail.
press home
expect size 105 1060x851
press show-all
expect size 105 1060x851
zoom 105
back
expect tile 104
expect size 105 1060x851
pause
resume
expect tile 104
expect size 105 1060x851
